*.md
*.markdown
CLAUDE.md
README.md
NOTES.md
ROADMAP.md
CHANGELOG.md
SPEC/
specs/
spec/
docs/
design/
plans/

# Infrastructure, ops and admin tooling (PUBLIC repo: local only, never pushed)
#
# This is a public repo. Anything describing how the box is administered, how
# it defends itself, or how to reach it is kept off it entirely: server configs,
# monitoring and watchdog scripts, the deploy listener, firewall and bot rules,
# SSH details, backups, dashboards. Publishing defensive thresholds tells an
# attacker exactly what to route around, and publishing host details narrows
# their search for free. Keep these locally and copy them to the VPS by hand.
#
# DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS, do not add these: Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml
# MUST stay tracked. The deploy pipeline runs `docker compose up -d --build`
# inside the repo checkout on the VPS, so ignoring them breaks production
# deploys outright. Neither contains a credential; .env is ignored separately.
nginx/
nginx*.conf
*.nginx
scripts/uptime-watch.sh
uptime-watch.sh
deploy-listener.js
deploy-run.sh
deploy.sh
*.service
*.timer
crontab*
ops/
infra/
runbooks/
backups/
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
known_hosts

# Playwright MCP verification artifacts (local debug only)
.playwright-mcp/
vr-org-*.png

# One-off article insert scripts the drafting pipeline leaves behind. They
# hardcode a single article body that already lives in data/articles.json,
# are not re-runnable, and write articles.json non-atomically. Scratch only.
/add_article*.py
